<settings version="2">
    <!-- Web server on with basic auth, so JSON-RPC is reachable at
         http://<box>:8080/jsonrpc as kodi/kodi. The whole fleet's tooling
         verifies boxes through this endpoint.

         ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: services.webserver comes LAST in this block.
         CNetworkServices::OnSettingChanging vetoes enabling the web server
         while authentication is on and the password is EMPTY - Kodi posts an
         OK dialog (string 36635, "a password must be entered as well") and
         the set returns false. A fresh box has auth on and no password, so
         enabling the server before setting the password fails outright.
         MEASURED on the first full bench run, 2026-08-30: the original
         webserver-first order cost that id a 20 s timeout and cascaded into
         two more refusals. Same rule as esenabled before esallinterfaces:
         parent and preconditions before the dependent.

         services.webserver is also CONFIRM-GATED on Kodi 22: enabling it
         fires a yes/no warning (string 36632) and the change is vetoed unless
         the answer is YES. The apply engine knows this id is gated and
         answers the confirm itself; see profile.CONFIRM_GATED and
         docs/settings-profile-experiments-2026-08-30.md. -->
    <setting id="services.webserverport">8080</setting>
    <setting id="services.webserverauthentication">true</setting>
    <setting id="services.webserverusername">kodi</setting>
    <setting id="services.webserverpassword">kodi</setting>
    <setting id="services.webserver">true</setting>

    <!-- "Allow remote control from applications on other systems".
         esallinterfaces is a no-op unless esenabled is also true. esenabled is
         already true by stock default, but pin it so a future Kodi flipping
         the default cannot silently break remote control. THIS true IS FOR
         fireos AND THE BENCH ONLY: overlays/tvos/settings.d/20-services.xml
         overrides it to false, the 2026-08-28 watchdog-kill workaround the
         owner approved as the recorded tvOS state. ORDER MATTERS:
         esenabled must be applied before esallinterfaces (parent before
         dependent), which is why it appears first here and why the loader
         keeps position-from-first when an overlay overrides a value.

         esallinterfaces is also CONFIRM-GATED (string 36633), and on top of
         that it restarts the JSON-RPC TCP server when it applies: setting it
         OVER remote TCP deadlocks that server against itself (measured on the
         bench, 2026-08-30, SIGKILL required). It is only ever set in-process. -->
    <setting id="services.esenabled">true</setting>
    <setting id="services.esallinterfaces">true</setting>

    <!-- Video cache buffer (Services > Caching), pinned to Kodi's own default
         on EVERY device class - the point is fleet convergence: before the pin
         the id floated across restore/flush cycles (archive 64, box 20,
         measured on atv1 during the 2026-08-30 restore-cycle proof). 20 is the
         ONLY value the loader accepts for this id (_kodisettings._PROFILE_MAY_PIN):
         it must equal the value every restore resets it to (KODI_DEFAULT_CACHE_MB)
         or the profile and the restore would flip-flop the fleet forever. The
         200-era raise is settled dead: docs/next-update-candidates.md item 1. -->
    <setting id="filecache.memorysize">20</setting>
</settings>
